- consider what happens when one packs actions into a tar file and deletes action files when bucse is running
- strange error when using ssh destination with no proper entry in authorized_keys present
- historic snapshot option
- docs:
 - README:
  - setup guide
  - example usage
  - comparison to other software
  - contribution guide
 - whitepaper
- correctly implement RENAME_EXCHANGE flag
- warning when using poor password strength (zxcvbn-c?)
- investigate a memory leak in libfuse when using fsstress
- handle addToDynArray failures
- improve local destination by applying a filesystem hook to be notified about changes in the filesystem
- s3 destination
- implement undo actions
- a client that reads an action file while another client is still uploading it rejects it and never reads it again until remount; write action files under a temporary name and rename when complete, or retry rejected files
- no fsync() in the local destination: after a power loss an action file may be saved without its blocks
- aes encryption backend (AES-256-CBC) has no integrity check (MAC); consider authenticated encryption, e.g. AES-GCM

Code review findings (2026-11-13), fix one by one:

Serious:
- [ ] 1. heap overflow on oversized action/storage/tar data from the server: decrypt
      functions don't check *outSize (bucse-mount.c:81, decryptBlock, tar.c:75) -- crypto-related, discuss first
- [x] 2. after a shrinking truncate the last block keeps its old length; later writes to it fail
      with EIO once the block is not cached (flush.c:116-127)
- [ ] 3. flushFile resets truncSize before I/O; a failed flush makes the next one truncate to 0 (flush.c:88-91)
- [ ] 4. ssh: sftp_write errors never detected (size_t res < 0, dest_ssh.c:197); sftp_close/fclose
      results unchecked -- action may point to a missing block
- [ ] 5. ssh tick: read error -1 passed on as a huge size_t (dest_ssh.c:802)
- [ ] 6. create.c:60 calls bucse_open_guarded() while holding bucseMutex -- deadlock
- [ ] 7. use-after-free of json tokener in error messages (bucse-mount.c:350/354, 434/438)
- [ ] 8. pthread_join on a never-created tickThread (bucse-mount.c:610)
- [ ] 9. int overflow for files > 2 GB (flush.c:220/286/309, truncate.c:76)
- [ ] 10. a remote EditFile drops local unflushed writes (actions.c:146-147); RemoveFile/RemoveDirectory
      free entries with pending writes/children

Medium:
- [ ] 11. read-only mode: O_RDONLY|O_TRUNC sets PendingTrunc (open.c:58); flushFile doesn't check confIsReadOnly()
- [ ] 12. actions sorted by time only (unstable qsort, microsecond timestamps); renameFile gives two actions
      the same time; dedup assumes identical actions are adjacent
- [ ] 13. AddDirectory doesn't check for an existing entry; out-of-order replay duplicates directories
- [ ] 14. renaming a dir onto an existing empty dir fails with EEXIST (rename.c:162)
- [ ] 15. serializeAction checks jsonNewAction instead of jsonNewContent (actions.c:553)
- [ ] 16. bucse-init ignores putRepositoryJsonFile result, exits 0 without a repository argument,
      misreports missing option arguments
- [ ] 17. action files that fail to open/read are still marked handled (both destinations)
- [ ] 18. terminal echo not restored when the passphrase fgets fails (bucse-mount.c:543)
- [ ] 19. "FUSE library version" prints the bucse version (bucse-mount.c:237)
- [ ] 20. design.md: a truncated CBC file doesn't always fail decryption (JSON parsing rejects it)
- [ ] 21. PBKDF2-SHA1 with 1 iteration -- crypto-related, discuss first
- [ ] 22. tests/allTests.sh doesn't run test9-test12; test9-test11 use unencrypted action files
      from tests/data, so they only work with -e none (allTests.sh uses aes); test11 fails until
      the "partially uploaded action never re-read" item above is fixed
- [ ] 24. test4 (5.2 GB cp) kills bucse-mount on a machine with 1.9 GB RAM, before any block is
      stored; suspected OOM: bucse_write buffers up to 10240 pending writes (~1.3 GB with 128 KB
      writes) before flushing. Look at it together with item 9. Note: test4/test5 also need
      ~16 GB of free disk.

Typos and misleading messages:
- [ ] 23. log message typos/copy-paste errors (dest_ssh.c, unlink.c, rmdir.c, actions.c, bucse-mount.c,
      create.c, filesystem.c, rename.c, flush.c, dest.h, encr.c, tar.c); add a printf format
      attribute to logPrintf and fix the %d/size_t mismatches it reports
